{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "39649204",
      "title": "Reacting to Events [Core Concept]",
      "sourceHash": "85f5759c5b5e8dca94424282fa34b3c9083a08dd60c28538d652dfd38bd53733",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.72,
          "end": 5.49,
          "en": "Now with those new TabButtons added here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.49,
          "end": 8.31,
          "en": "the next step, of course, is to make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.31,
          "end": 11.82,
          "en": "that once we click them, something happens.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.82,
          "end": 14.28,
          "en": "And of course the ultimate goal is to then",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 14.28,
          "end": 17.58,
          "en": "show different content below these buttons",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.58,
          "end": 18.963,
          "en": "when they are clicked.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.28,
          "end": 21.75,
          "en": "Now, for that, we can first of all",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.75,
          "end": 24.18,
          "en": "go to that TabButton component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24.18,
          "end": 28.35,
          "en": "because that's where we have the native button element,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 28.35,
          "end": 30.48,
          "en": "the build-in button element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 30.48,
          "end": 33.81,
          "en": "And let's now start by adding a click event listener",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 33.81,
          "end": 34.833,
          "en": "to this button.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 35.94,
          "end": 38.85,
          "en": "Now, in regular JavaScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 38.85,
          "end": 42.93,
          "en": "you would typically try to select this button,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 42.93,
          "end": 46.17,
          "en": "for example with querySelector button,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 46.17,
          "end": 48.78,
          "en": "and you could then add an event listener",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 48.78,
          "end": 51.57,
          "en": "with the addEventListener method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 51.57,
          "end": 54.15,
          "en": "And with that you could listen to the click event",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 54.15,
          "end": 58.83,
          "en": "for example, and then define a function, for example",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 58.83,
          "end": 61.35,
          "en": "such an anonymous arrow function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 61.35,
          "end": 64.35,
          "en": "that should be triggered when that button is clicked.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 64.35,
          "end": 69.03,
          "en": "That's how you would do it in vanilla JavaScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 69.03,
          "end": 74.03,
          "en": "But of course here we are not in vanilla JavaScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 74.37,
          "end": 77.25,
          "en": "Instead here we're in a React project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 77.25,
          "end": 79.98,
          "en": "And when working with React,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 79.98,
          "end": 83.13,
          "en": "as you learned in the first course section,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 83.13,
          "end": 86.91,
          "en": "we don't want to write imperative code like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 86.91,
          "end": 89.25,
          "en": "Instead, we want to write declarative code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 89.25,
          "end": 93.96000000000001,
          "en": "And therefore, when working with React as a developer,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 93.96000000000001,
          "end": 97.2,
          "en": "we really don't wanna start interacting",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 97.2,
          "end": 101.4,
          "en": "with the DOM and with the page with code like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 101.4,
          "end": 104.03999999999999,
          "en": "Instead, we wanna let React do that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 104.03999999999999,
          "end": 107.7,
          "en": "And therefore, in React, you instead add event listeners",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 107.7,
          "end": 111.21000000000001,
          "en": "to elements by adding a special attribute,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 111.21000000000001,
          "end": 114.57,
          "en": "a special prop to those elements.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 114.57,
          "end": 118.8,
          "en": "And I'm calling it a prop here as well, because in the end",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 118.8,
          "end": 122.91,
          "en": "those built-in elements are also just components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 122.91,
          "end": 125.64,
          "en": "Just components, that are already provided",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 125.64,
          "end": 129.06,
          "en": "and understood by React, you could say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 129.06,
          "end": 131.12,
          "en": "And the special prop you want to add here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 131.12,
          "end": 133.83,
          "en": "is the onClick prop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 133.83,
          "end": 138.82999999999998,
          "en": "And these built-in elements support many on-something props.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 139.02,
          "end": 142.5,
          "en": "As you can see, if you just type on and you then",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 142.5,
          "end": 147.36,
          "en": "open this suggestion menu by pressing Ctrl + Space.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 147.36,
          "end": 150.32999999999998,
          "en": "You will see many on props in there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 150.32999999999998,
          "end": 152.28,
          "en": "which in the end allow you to listen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 152.28,
          "end": 155.1,
          "en": "to a broad variety of events.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 155.1,
          "end": 159.21,
          "en": "Now of course, not all props here and all events make sense",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 159.21,
          "end": 163.05,
          "en": "for all elements and all use cases, but as you can see",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 163.05,
          "end": 164.76,
          "en": "there is a broad variety of events",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 164.76,
          "end": 166.53,
          "en": "you can listen to in theory.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 166.53,
          "end": 168.18,
          "en": "And here it's the click event,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 168.18,
          "end": 170.553,
          "en": "so it's the onClick prop I want to add.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 171.57,
          "end": 174.03,
          "en": "You can also not just add that on a button,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 174.03,
          "end": 176.13,
          "en": "but really on any element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 176.13,
          "end": 178.74,
          "en": "I could also add this onClick prop here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 178.74,
          "end": 180.75,
          "en": "to the list item.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 180.75,
          "end": 185.19,
          "en": "Now the value for this onClick prop here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 185.19,
          "end": 190.11,
          "en": "or actually for any event prop, is a function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 190.11,
          "end": 193.98,
          "en": "So the value you should provide here should be a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 193.98,
          "end": 196.71,
          "en": "because you want to point at the function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 196.71,
          "end": 200.163,
          "en": "that should be executed when that event here occurs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 201,
          "end": 204.36,
          "en": "And therefore here we could add such a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 204.36,
          "end": 207.12,
          "en": "and we can define this function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 207.12,
          "end": 209.46,
          "en": "inside of a component function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 209.46,
          "end": 212.64,
          "en": "because that is something you are allowed to do",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 212.64,
          "end": 214.2,
          "en": "in JavaScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 214.2,
          "end": 217.86,
          "en": "You can define functions inside of functions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 217.86,
          "end": 222.21,
          "en": "and those inner functions will then only be callable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 222.21,
          "end": 224.55,
          "en": "from inside this function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 224.55,
          "end": 226.17000000000002,
          "en": "which is absolutely fine here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 226.17000000000002,
          "end": 229.29,
          "en": "because we want to use this inner function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 229.29,
          "end": 232.59,
          "en": "as a value for this onClick prop here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 232.59,
          "end": 234.84,
          "en": "So here we could add a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 234.84,
          "end": 237.423,
          "en": "that could be called handleClick.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 238.5,
          "end": 241.8,
          "en": "The function name, of course, is up to you,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 241.8,
          "end": 245.4,
          "en": "but it is quite common to use such a name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 245.4,
          "end": 248.01,
          "en": "for functions that should be triggered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 248.01,
          "end": 250.11,
          "en": "when certain events occur.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 250.11,
          "end": 254.4,
          "en": "So starting with handle and then the name of the event",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 254.4,
          "end": 257.34,
          "en": "for which this function should be triggered.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 257.34,
          "end": 259.14,
          "en": "This is not a must do,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 259.14,
          "end": 261.6,
          "en": "you could name this anything you want,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 261.6,
          "end": 263.91,
          "en": "but this is a convention.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 263.91,
          "end": 266.64,
          "en": "An alternative, which you'll also see quite a bit,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 266.64,
          "end": 269.85,
          "en": "is basically this way of writing it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 269.85,
          "end": 272.01,
          "en": "where you have the event name first",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 272.01,
          "end": 274.263,
          "en": "and then handler thereafter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 275.58,
          "end": 278.52,
          "en": "But here I'll use handleClick.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 278.52,
          "end": 281.7,
          "en": "And for the moment I'll just add a console.log statement",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 281.7,
          "end": 286.26,
          "en": "in there where I console.log, \"Hello World!\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 286.26,
          "end": 289.92,
          "en": "Now we have to use this handleClick function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 289.92,
          "end": 293.103,
          "en": "as a value for the onClick prop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 293.97,
          "end": 298.11,
          "en": "And what's really important here is that handleClick,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 298.11,
          "end": 302.79,
          "en": "down here in line eight, must not be executed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 302.79,
          "end": 306.69,
          "en": "You must not add these parentheses here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 306.69,
          "end": 309.84,
          "en": "Instead, you just want to use the name of the function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 309.84,
          "end": 313.35,
          "en": "because you want to use the function as a value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 313.35,
          "end": 317.61,
          "en": "It is the value that's passed to the onClick prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 317.61,
          "end": 321.36,
          "en": "because this function here should not be executed by you,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 321.36,
          "end": 325.56,
          "en": "which would be the case if you would add these parentheses,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 325.56,
          "end": 328.56,
          "en": "but instead it should be executed by React",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 328.56,
          "end": 330.72,
          "en": "when a click on this button occurs,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 330.72,
          "end": 332.673,
          "en": "so at some point in the future.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 333.81,
          "end": 335.79,
          "en": "If you would add parentheses here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 335.79,
          "end": 338.31,
          "en": "this function would get executed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 338.31,
          "end": 341.76,
          "en": "when this line of code here gets executed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 341.76,
          "end": 343.40999999999997,
          "en": "And that will be the case",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 343.40999999999997,
          "end": 346.86,
          "en": "when this overall component function gets executed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 346.86,
          "end": 351.21,
          "en": "and when this JSX code here gets rendered to the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 351.21,
          "end": 352.86,
          "en": "And that's not the point of time",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 352.86,
          "end": 354.84000000000003,
          "en": "where this function should be executed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 354.84000000000003,
          "end": 356.90999999999997,
          "en": "Instead, it should be executed, when the button",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 356.90999999999997,
          "end": 359.7,
          "en": "is clicked, by React, under the hood,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 359.7,
          "end": 362.7,
          "en": "and therefore we just use the function name here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 362.7,
          "end": 365.1,
          "en": "we use the function as a value, therefore,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 365.1,
          "end": 369.21,
          "en": "and we pass that function as a value to onClick.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 369.21,
          "end": 372.39,
          "en": "And with that, if you save that file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 372.39,
          "end": 375.33,
          "en": "if you open your developer tools",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 375.33,
          "end": 378.21,
          "en": "and you click on one of these buttons,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 378.21,
          "end": 379.95,
          "en": "you see, \"Hello World!\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 379.95,
          "end": 383.58,
          "en": "And you'll see that this gets printed again and again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 383.58,
          "end": 386.25,
          "en": "as you can tell by this incrementing number here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 386.25,
          "end": 388.293,
          "en": "whenever you click any button.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 389.19,
          "end": 392.25,
          "en": "So this is how you can listen to events,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 392.25,
          "end": 396.24,
          "en": "how you can react to events in your React projects.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 396.24,
          "end": 399.27,
          "en": "And this is therefore the first important step",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 399.27,
          "end": 403.503,
          "en": "towards our goal of making this app a bit more interactive.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}